#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
patch_L414_1_scanner_window_20261009.py -- the provenance scanner reads
a row's own comment block, names declared rows, and prints the push
gate's number by name (L-414, the scanner's window).

HOW TO RUN: save this file in the orrery folder (the one holding
PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md and LEDGER_CONSOLIDATED.md), open it in VS Code
and click Run. From a terminal the command is

    python patch_L414_1_scanner_window_20261009.py

It asks nothing. It reads every file first, checks each one is the
version it was built against, makes every edit in memory, and writes
only if every check passed. Then it runs skills_index.py twice -- once
to write provenance-discipline's read plan and the protocol's manifest
row, once with --check -- and prints both.

WHAT IT DOES

1. provenance_scanner.py: a row in constants_new.py is read through its
   own comment block, not a window of 30 lines back and 15 ahead. A
   declared row with its reason written down is listed by name and
   never counts as Tier-1. The run ends with a GATE PATH line: the
   Tier-1 findings on what leaves the orrery (data/constants_export.json
   and data/objects_export.json), each named. The audit gains a Gate
   Path section and a Declared Rows section.
2. provenance_history.py: each run record carries the gate-path
   findings by name, and the delta says which entered and which left.
3. test_row_run.py (new): 16 pins for the above.
4. orrery_maintenance_run.py: runs the new pins as "Scanner row run
   (L-414)", and quotes the scanner's GATE PATH line in its summary.
5. provenance-discipline 2.27 -> 2.28 (SKILL.md and its field notes);
   its v2.25 entry moves to documentation/SKILL_HISTORIES.md.
6. PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md v3.87; v3.84 moves to
   documentation/PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS_HISTORY.md PART 1.
7. LEDGER_CONSOLIDATED.md (L-414, the new L-427, L-351, L-184, the
   header stamp), documentation/WHERE_WE_ARE.md (by section; nothing
   below the run-record marker), and the session's handoff (new).

SUCCESS: one "ok" line per edit, "patch applied", and skills_index.py
ending "OK: 12 skills parsed".
FAILURE: "ERROR:" or "ANCHOR FAIL:" and "NOTHING was written."
Running it a second time refuses and writes nothing.
Undo is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

WHAT IS PERMANENT: the scanner's row rule, the gate-path figure, the
history's names, test_row_run.py and the skill text. The script itself
is spent once it has run; move it to documentation/.

Files Tony annotates -- the ledger, Where We Are, and the history
files -- are checked only at the lines edited, never by a fingerprint
of the whole file (L-419). The protocol is checked the same way,
because skills_index.py rewrites its manifest zone.

Built on orrery aa46bb10 at https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery
(branch main). Written October 9, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
